submittedPrompt:
Calculate the average electric power consumption in African countries with power stations capacity above 1000MW

Task conventions: Use CONTINENT=Africa on supplied countries. A qualifying country strictly contains at least one supplied power-station point whose DsgAttr02 capacity is strictly greater than 1000 MW. Use the original country polygon, not a clipped boundary; no operating-status restriction. Calculate the unweighted mean of 2014 WDI EG.USE.ELEC.KH.PC values (kWh per capita) for qualifying countries with known data, one observation per country, not one per station. 2014 is the latest populated year in the frozen table. Join by ISO_A3/Country Code; missing values remain unknown. Maps are optional.

Some supplied power-station records lack geometry. They cannot satisfy a spatial relationship; do not assign them using a country-name guess. Disclose this coverage limitation and add unlocated_count to the final JSON: the number of capacity-above-1000MW station records without a usable location. The country selection and mean describe located qualifying records only.

Produce an inspectable contributing-country artifact with 2014 consumption, original geometry and benchmark_row_id. End with one fenced JSON object: {count: contributing countries with known consumption, unknown_count: qualifying countries missing consumption, coverage_note: string, selection: {collectionId, itemId, assetKey}, metrics: {mean: number}, value_field: name_of_consumption_column_in_selection}. Explain the average and units in prose.

Delivery format: submit the structured answer through the final-result tool and finish with a matching concise response. [Product-specific tool arguments omitted.]

